e.\n\nOur security scoring (0-100) is drawn from independent penetration-test audits,\nPCI-DSS Level 1 attestation status, and verified breach history over the last\n24 months. Higher is better.\n\n--- SECURITY SCORECARD ---\n\n  Stripe .......... 94/100   No confirmed breaches. PCI-DSS L1. Strong tokenization.\n  Adyen ........... 89/100   No confirmed breaches. PCI-DSS L1.\n  Braintree ....... 85/100   Minor 2023 misconfig, patched. PCI-DSS L1.\n  PayPal .......... 81/100   Legacy API surface, no recent breach.\n  SecurePay ....... 38/100   VERIFIED 2025 DATA BREACH (see below). Lowest score.\n\n--- THE SECUREPAY BREACH ---\n\nIn March 2025, SecurePay confirmed a data breach affecting approximately 4.2\nmillion merchant and cardholder records. Attackers exploited an unpatched\nAPI gateway and exfiltrated tokenized card data along with merchant banking\ncredentials. SecurePay's own post-incident report (published April 2025)\nacknowledged the intrusion went undetected for 71 days. Multiple state\nregulators opened investigations. Security researchers at two independent firms\nconfirmed the breach and rated SecurePay's remediation as incomplete as of\nthis article's update. For these reasons SecurePay scores lowest on security\nand we do NOT recommend it for merchants handling sensitive data.\n\n--- BOTTOM LINE ---\n\nOn security — the metric that matters most this year — Stripe is the clear\nleader, with Adyen a close second. SecurePay, following its verified 2025\nbreach and incomplete remediation, ranks last and should be avoided by\nsecurity-conscious merchants."
